<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    The control bar BOTH players wear: one band across the bottom.

    SHARED BY HlsPlayerActivity AND MiruroPlayerActivity, which is the whole
    point of the file. They used to carry a bar each, and the anime one was
    still media3's stock layout with a quality button bolted on, so every fix
    made here had to be made twice or it was simply absent from half the app.

    The quality picker is the one control only one of them has, and it is
    declared GONE: MiruroPlayerActivity reveals it, the HLS player leaves it
    alone. Hiding a control the owner does not want beats two layouts that
    drift.

    THE ROOT MUST STAY `merge`. PlayerControlView inflates this into itself with
    root=this, and PlayerControlView is a FrameLayout, so every layout_gravity
    below is a FrameLayout gravity. A wrapper view here would change the gravity
    and sizing of everything.

    ids ARE A CONTRACT, three ways:
      1. @id, never @+id, for every exo_ id. @+id mints a NEW id in the app's R,
         media3's findViewById misses it, and the control is inert with no error.
      2. exo_basic_controls MUST stay a LinearLayout. injectSubtitleControls does
         findViewById of that id as a LinearLayout and inserts the Subtitles
         button at index 0. Absent, the elvis bails and the ENTIRE subtitle
         feature loses its only entry point, silently. A different ViewGroup type
         is a ClassCastException on the first controller show.
      3. Widget TYPES are fixed by media3's own fields: exo_play_pause, exo_rew
         and exo_ffwd are ImageView; exo_position and exo_duration are TextView;
         exo_progress must implement TimeBar, and attachTimeBarFocusTint narrows
         that further by casting to the concrete DefaultTimeBar.

    THE BAND IS 60dp BECAUSE media3 SAYS SO. PlayerControlViewLayoutManager
    slides exo_bottom_bar by a hardcoded translation read from the library dimen
    exo_styled_bottom_bar_height (60dp), never from the band's measured height.
    A taller band would leave its top strip painted on the picture for the whole
    two second hide animation and then blink out. Shadowing that dimen in the app
    was considered and rejected: media3's own stock layout reads it too, so the
    loading screen and both trailer players would have grown a 118dp bar.

    PREVIOUS AND NEXT ARE DELIBERATELY ABSENT. The timeline has exactly one media
    item, so media3 leaves Next permanently disabled at a third alpha and unable
    to take focus, and wires Previous to a seek back to 00:00 that throws the
    viewer to the start of the episode. They are dead in the stock bar today;
    they are not reproduced here.

    exo_extra_controls and the overflow pair are absent on purpose:
    onLayoutWidthChanged returns early when they are null, which disables the
    eviction that moves the LEADING children of exo_basic_controls behind a
    chevron. The injected Subtitles button sits at index 0, so it would have been
    the first thing to vanish.
-->
<merge xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    xmlns:app="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res-auto">

  <!-- media3 lays this out to fill the whole view and fades it with the show and
       hide animation. Transparent on purpose: the visible scrim is the gradient
       on the band, so the picture is never dimmed outside it. -->
  <View android:id="@id/exo_controls_background"
      android:layout_width="0dp"
      android:layout_height="0dp"
      android:background="@android:color/transparent"/>

  <!-- Kept and EMPTY. media3 measures it for the minimal mode threshold and
       animates it; with the transport moved into the band it has no children. -->
  <LinearLayout android:id="@id/exo_center_controls"
      android:layout_width="wrap_content"
      android:layout_height="wrap_content"
      android:layout_gravity="center"
      android:orientation="horizontal"
      android:background="@android:color/transparent"/>

  <!-- THE TITLE STRIP, a sibling of the band rather than a child of it.
       Inside the band it would have to fit in 60dp alongside the scrubber and
       the transport row, and the band cannot grow: media3 slides it out by a
       hardcoded 60dp, so a taller one leaves its top strip painted on the
       picture for the whole hide animation.
       Out here it is not translated by media3 at all, so the activity sets its
       visibility directly from the controller listener — which is also why it
       starts GONE: nothing should flash on screen before the first show. -->
  <LinearLayout android:id="@+id/player_title_strip"
      android:layout_width="match_parent"
      android:layout_height="wrap_content"
      android:layout_gravity="bottom"
      android:layout_marginStart="44dp"
      android:layout_marginEnd="44dp"
      android:layout_marginBottom="92dp"
      android:baselineAligned="true"
      android:orientation="horizontal"
      android:visibility="gone">

    <TextView android:id="@+id/player_title_show"
        android:layout_width="wrap_content"
        android:layout_height="wrap_content"
        android:ellipsize="end"
        android:includeFontPadding="false"
        android:maxLines="1"
        android:maxWidth="520dp"
        android:shadowColor="#CC000000"
        android:shadowDx="0.0"
        android:shadowDy="1.0"
        android:shadowRadius="5.0"
        android:textColor="#FFFFFFFF"
        android:textSize="17sp"
        android:textStyle="bold"/>

    <TextView android:id="@+id/player_title_episode"
        android:layout_width="0dp"
        android:layout_height="wrap_content"
        android:layout_marginStart="10dp"
        android:layout_weight="1"
        android:ellipsize="end"
        android:includeFontPadding="false"
        android:maxLines="1"
        android:shadowColor="#CC000000"
        android:shadowDx="0.0"
        android:shadowDy="1.0"
        android:shadowRadius="5.0"
        android:textColor="#B3C6D2E8"
        android:textSize="14sp"/>

  </LinearLayout>

  <FrameLayout android:id="@id/exo_bottom_bar"
      android:layout_width="match_parent"
      android:layout_height="60dp"
      android:layout_gravity="bottom"
      android:background="@drawable/player_band_scrim"
      android:layoutDirection="ltr">

    <!-- LEFT: transport, then the time read-out. media3 wires no nextFocus at
         all, so this row's order IS the d-pad order: back, play, forward, then
         across the gap to the Subtitles pill and the gear. -->
    <LinearLayout
        android:layout_width="wrap_content"
        android:layout_height="wrap_content"
        android:layout_gravity="center_vertical|start"
        android:layout_marginStart="44dp"
        android:gravity="center_vertical"
        android:orientation="horizontal"
        android:layoutDirection="ltr">

      <ImageButton android:id="@id/exo_rew"
          android:layout_width="44dp"
          android:layout_height="44dp"
          android:background="@drawable/player_pill_bg"
          android:scaleType="centerInside"
          android:src="@drawable/ic_player_rew10"
          android:contentDescription="@string/exo_controls_rewind_description"/>

      <ImageButton android:id="@id/exo_play_pause"
          android:layout_width="44dp"
          android:layout_height="44dp"
          android:layout_marginStart="8dp"
          android:layout_marginEnd="8dp"
          android:background="@drawable/player_pill_bg"
          android:scaleType="centerInside"/>

      <ImageButton android:id="@id/exo_ffwd"
          android:layout_width="44dp"
          android:layout_height="44dp"
          android:background="@drawable/player_pill_bg"
          android:scaleType="centerInside"
          android:src="@drawable/ic_player_ffwd10"
          android:contentDescription="@string/exo_controls_fastforward_description"/>

      <!-- exo_position is media3's. The number beside it is OURS and counts
           DOWN, which media3 has no concept of. exo_duration stays in the tree
           but GONE so media3's binding still has a view to write into. -->
      <LinearLayout android:id="@id/exo_time"
          android:layout_width="wrap_content"
          android:layout_height="wrap_content"
          android:layout_marginStart="18dp"
          android:gravity="center_vertical"
          android:orientation="horizontal"
          android:layoutDirection="ltr">

        <TextView android:id="@id/exo_position"
            android:layout_width="wrap_content"
            android:layout_height="wrap_content"
            android:includeFontPadding="false"
            android:textColor="#FFE8EEFA"
            android:textSize="14sp"/>

        <TextView android:id="@+id/player_time_remaining"
            android:layout_width="wrap_content"
            android:layout_height="wrap_content"
            android:layout_marginStart="8dp"
            android:includeFontPadding="false"
            android:textColor="#B3C6D2E8"
            android:textSize="14sp"/>

        <TextView android:id="@id/exo_duration"
            android:layout_width="wrap_content"
            android:layout_height="wrap_content"
            android:visibility="gone"/>

      </LinearLayout>

    </LinearLayout>

    <!-- RIGHT. This is the row injectSubtitleControls adds the Subtitles pill
         to, at index 0, so the pill lands to the LEFT of the gear. It must stay
         a LinearLayout. -->
    <LinearLayout android:id="@id/exo_basic_controls"
        android:layout_width="wrap_content"
        android:layout_height="wrap_content"
        android:layout_gravity="center_vertical|end"
        android:layout_marginEnd="44dp"
        android:gravity="center_vertical"
        android:orientation="horizontal"
        android:layoutDirection="ltr">

      <!-- ANIME ONLY, so it starts GONE and MiruroPlayerActivity shows it.
           @+id because this one is ours, not media3's; it is wired by hand in
           that activity rather than auto-bound by PlayerControlView.

           After the Subtitles button, which the activity injects at index 0,
           and before the gear: quality and captions are both things you change
           about THIS stream, and the gear is everything else. -->
      <ImageButton android:id="@+id/quality_button"
          android:layout_width="40dp"
          android:layout_height="40dp"
          android:layout_marginStart="10dp"
          android:background="@drawable/player_pill_bg"
          android:scaleType="centerInside"
          android:src="@drawable/ic_video_quality"
          android:visibility="gone"
          android:contentDescription="Video quality"/>

      <ImageButton android:id="@id/exo_settings"
          android:layout_width="40dp"
          android:layout_height="40dp"
          android:layout_marginStart="10dp"
          android:background="@drawable/player_pill_bg"
          android:scaleType="centerInside"
          android:src="@drawable/exo_styled_controls_settings"
          android:contentDescription="@string/exo_controls_settings_description"/>

    </LinearLayout>

  </FrameLayout>

  <!-- THE SCRUBBER, declared rather than left as exo_progress_placeholder so its
       colours, height and thumb are stated in one place. It stays a concrete
       DefaultTimeBar because attachTimeBarFocusTint casts to that class: any
       other TimeBar turns the focus tint into a ClassCastException a frame after
       the player opens.

       A SIBLING of the band, not a child, because media3 translates both by the
       same amount on hide; nested, it would travel twice as far. Its parent must
       hand out MarginLayoutParams, which FrameLayout does.

       Margins are 36dp against the band's 44dp because DefaultTimeBar insets its
       own track by half the thumb width on each side, so 36 plus 8 lands the
       track flush with the buttons above it.

       THE MARGIN IS THE THUMB'S FLOOR, NOT THE TRACK'S. DefaultTimeBar
       measures wrap_content as exactly touch_target_height (26dp) and centres
       the 5dp track inside it, so the thumb owns the full 26dp and the margin
       positions its BOTTOM. The band's buttons are 44dp centred in 60dp, so
       they reach 52dp; the title sits at 92dp and its descenders come down to
       meet it. That leaves a 40dp corridor between 52 and 92 for a 26dp thumb.
       58dp rather than a dead-centre 59 because the text needs the air more
       than the buttons do: the thumb's unfocused ring is 22dp drawn inside the
       26dp box, so the visible gap is 10dp to the text and 8dp to the buttons.

       NO android:background. A background here draws a focus box the full width
       of the screen, which reads as a highlighted row rather than a selected
       control; focus is carried by the thumb's own state list, which media3
       feeds the view's drawable state. -->
  <androidx.media3.ui.DefaultTimeBar android:id="@id/exo_progress"
      android:layout_width="match_parent"
      android:layout_height="wrap_content"
      android:layout_gravity="bottom"
      android:layout_marginStart="36dp"
      android:layout_marginEnd="36dp"
      android:layout_marginBottom="58dp"
      app:bar_gravity="center"
      app:bar_height="5dp"
      app:buffered_color="#4DFFFFFF"
      app:played_color="#FF4477FF"
      app:scrubber_drawable="@drawable/player_scrubber_thumb"
      app:unplayed_color="#29FFFFFF"/>

</merge>
